{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Gnusto game is a value and a play session is a function of its typed input, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the natural test is a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"transcript test"}]},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},{"type":"text","text":" boots"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns everything printed with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input interleaved as "},{"code":"> command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the same text the player saw. Everything else","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in this library either cuts that string down to the part a claim is about, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records a Swift Testing issue with the whole of it attached, which is what a bare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#expect(transcript.contains(…))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot do. Gnusto’s own suite is roughly a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thousand tests of this shape.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle nor a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". It declares no verbs,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no rules and no entities, and a game never links it: it is a test-only helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library, and it imports the toolchain’s Testing library, which ships with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler rather than the OS. Put it in a test target’s dependencies and nowhere"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else — an executable that links it can fail at load time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host passes a game type and a list of commands; the library holds one piece"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of state of its own, a process-wide cache of prepared games behind a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mutex"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},{"text":" exists because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bootstrap.build"},{"text":" reflects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the game and every content bundle it lists, and that runs about 15× longer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a turn does. The suite boots the same handful of game types thousands of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"times, so building each once and copying the prepared definition takes bootstrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out of the suite’s critical path. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"play"},{"text":" goes through it; a test that wants the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world rather than the transcript can call it directly and drive ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"REPL"},{"text":" itself.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gnusto catalog’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Testing Your Game"}]},{"type":"text","text":" article teaches four of these helpers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the habits around them — pinning a seed, sweeping "},{"code":"GNUSTO_SEED","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that pass by luck, deciding when a trap is worth a test at all. This page is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it stops short of."}]},{"text":"A transcript test","type":"heading","anchor":"A-transcript-test","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","@Test func ringingTheBellWinsTheGame() async throws {","    let transcript = try await play(","        MyGame(),","        [\"take rope\", \"north\", \"ring bell\"],","        seed: 7)","","    expectInOrder(","        transcript,","        [","            \"Village Garden\",","            \"Taken.\",","            \"Bell Tower\",","            \"The great bronze bell peals\",","        ])","","    let looking = turnOutput(of: \"examine hook\", in: transcript)","    #expect(looking.contains(\"screwed to the wall\"))","    #expect(occurrences(of: \"The bell tolls\", in: transcript) == 1)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Omit ","type":"text"},{"code":"seed:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the stream is fresh each run, unless ","type":"text"},{"code":"GNUSTO_SEED","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is set,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which pins every call that passed no seed of its own and leaves the ones that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"did alone. Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"saveDirectory:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when a test exercises named ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"save"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it never writes to the real per-user saves directory."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Slicing before asserting","anchor":"Slicing-before-asserting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"turnOutput(of:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" matches the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" occurrence of a command, so a route"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that types "},{"code":"look","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" four times wants four different commands or a different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"helper. "},{"code":"output(after:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"output(before:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cut on any marker rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a prompt, which is the slice for “and then, later…”. "},{"code":"occurrences(of:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the count assertion — a beat that must fire exactly once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"lines(mentioning:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the matching lines in transcript order, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what an alignment check compares between two runs to prove that a guard burned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"no randomness.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Asserting","anchor":"Asserting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"text":" is the workhorse: a sequence of substrings, each match resuming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"after the last, strict enough to pin the beats that matter and loose enough to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"survive an edit between them. The rest of the assertions are about a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript rather than a phrase in it. "},{"code":"expectEveryNounAnswered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on either"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"answer a game gives a noun it doesn’t know — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"I don't know the word \"x\""},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You can't see any such thing"},{"text":" — which is what a walk of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x <noun>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"room’s own description is checking. ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectNoAmbiguity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fails on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which do you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mean…"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", and is deliberately a separate call: an unanswered noun is always a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defect, while an ambiguity is only one where the author believed the room held a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"single thing of that kind.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives"},{"text":" is for a game that has re-voiced the stub verbs","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and wants to keep the claim whole. It reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.stubs"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"type":"text","text":" rather"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"than naming the properties, so a stub added to the engine tomorrow is compared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the day it lands. "},{"code":"engineVoicedStubLines","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same sweep without the issue","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recording, split out so the sweep itself can be tested for being alive — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection loop that matches nothing passes silently."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Trapping a `fatalError`","anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine answers an authoring mistake by crashing with a message that names"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"it. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fatalError"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be caught, so the only way to assert on one is to run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it in a child process and read what it printed; Swift Testing’s exit tests do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the running and "},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does the reading.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let result = await #expect(processExitsWith: .failure, observing: [\\.standardErrorContent]) {","    _ = try await play(MyGame(), [\"prime the bomb\"])","}","expectTrap(result, says: \"names a daemon\", \"use startDaemon(_:)\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call is a child process, some 60 ms against 1 ms for an in-process","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assertion, and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#expect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has to stay at the call site because its body is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"compiled into a C function that captures nothing. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectTrap"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own doc comment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carries the rule for when that is worth spending, since it is where the person"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deciding is standing: make the bad message unrepresentable and write no test,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"or split the message into a pure function and assert it in a millisecond, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaching for the third shape. Exit tests are built on macOS, Linux and Windows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and are absent elsewhere, so "},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is compiled under "},{"code":"GNUSTO_EXIT_TESTS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and a test using it wants a "},{"code":"#if","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a suite that also runs on iOS, watchOS,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tvOS, visionOS or WASI.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GnustoTestSupport"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"GnustoTestSupport","externalID":"GnustoTestSupport","role":"collection"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Playing a session","anchor":"Playing-a-session","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"]},{"title":"Slicing a transcript","anchor":"Slicing-a-transcript","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(after:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)"]},{"title":"Asserting","anchor":"Asserting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"]},{"title":"Trapping a `fatalError`","anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport"},"references":{"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"expectEveryNounAnswered","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expecteverynounanswered(_:_:sourcelocation:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a Swift Testing issue if the transcript contains either answer a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"game gives to a noun it doesn’t know: "},{"code":"I don't know the word \"x\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a word","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outside the vocabulary, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You can't see any such thing"},{"text":" for a word the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parser knows only as an adjective, or for a thing that isn’t in scope.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)":{"type":"topic","title":"cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Builds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameWorld"},{"type":"text","text":" from a per-type-cached "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreparedGame"},{"text":", so repeated boots","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the same game across the suite pay "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bootstrap.build"},{"type":"text","text":" only once. The world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is otherwise identical to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameWorld(game:seed:saveDirectory:)"},{"text":": it copies the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"shared value-type definition and pristine state and applies its own seed, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"worlds never share mutable state."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/cachedworld(_:seed:savedirectory:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cachedWorld","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP","text":"Game","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"seed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt64V","text":"UInt64"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saveDirectory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","text":"URL","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GameWorld","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9GameWorldC"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Boots a game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns the full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript — every line the game printed, with the player’s input"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interleaved as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> command"},{"type":"text","text":" the way a player would see it."}],"type":"topic","title":"play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/play(_:_:seed:savedirectory:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"play"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Game"},{"kind":"text","text":", ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"seed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt64V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt64"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"saveDirectory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/occurrences(of:in:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","abstract":[{"text":"How many times ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"needle"},{"text":" occurs in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"haystack"},{"type":"text","text":" — the count assertions in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"transcript tests are usually about (“this beat fires exactly once”)."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"occurrences","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sy","text":"StringProtocol"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","title":"occurrences(of:in:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/output(before:in:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/output(before:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything a transcript printed before its first occurrence of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"marker"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"output"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"before"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","title":"output(before:in:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport","kind":"symbol","title":"GnustoTestSupport","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)":{"type":"topic","title":"engineVoicedStubLines(in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every stub-verb line a game still answers in the engine’s voice, by property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/enginevoicedstublines(in:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"engineVoicedStubLines","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"StubReplies","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV11StubRepliesV"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"}